  "changelog_section_fixed": "Fixes",
  "changelog_section_security": "Security",
  "changelog_v2_0_1_bullet_1": "Picking the date and time of tasks, reminders and events is quicker: the calendar and the time are in the same window, so changing just the time (or just the day) takes a single tap.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_1": "Completely redesigned app: notes, tasks and calendar in one place, synced to your account.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_2": "Notes with custom styles, Markdown, checklists, audio notes, links between notes, website links you open with a tap and 6 ready-made templates. In Settings > Notes, choose whether the + button opens the menu (note, list, task, audio, template) or creates a note right away.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_3": "Tasks with subtasks, repeats and starred tasks: set the day, time and details right when you create them. The list is grouped by day (Today, Tomorrow, later dates, then tasks without a date). Tap a task to see all its details, and from there complete it, tick its subtasks or edit it with the pencil. For a repeating task, choose whether to delete just this one or the following ones too.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_4": "New calendar with Day, Week, Month, Year and Schedule views: an hour column with a current-time line, a Schedule you can scroll freely into the past and future, and your chosen view is remembered. It also shows tasks with a date (you can hide them), birthdays and name days, and imports and exports ICS files. The + button creates an event or a task, and events can have a place you open in Maps and a card color.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_5": "A clearer calendar: each kind of entry (event, all-day event, birthday, name day, task) has its own pastel color, birthdays and name days get festive cards with confetti, and tasks show their icon. Choosing Birthday or Name day instantly makes the event yearly, all-day and with alerts.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_6": "Simple notifications: tasks and events with a time alert you at that time; all-day events, birthdays and name days alert you on the day and/or the day before, at the time set in Settings. Notes can have a reminder. Tapping a notification opens the linked item, permission is asked only for the first alert, and picking a time for today starts from the current time.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_7": "Labels saved to your account, added from the editor and tapped to see the notes that use them. Archive and trash with automatic deletion after 7 days: deleting from the editor moves to the trash, and after archiving or trashing you can tap Undo.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_8": "Swipe a task right to complete it or left to trash it; in list view, swipe a note to archive or trash it. Pull down to refresh the lists and, if syncing fails, tap Retry.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_9": "Everything in Settings > Backup & data: manual and automatic backups you restore with a tap, which also save labels and settings, and note export to PDF, TXT, JSON, CSV and HTML.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_10": "Offline mode: changes made without a connection are saved on the device and sent as soon as you are back online, with a notice while they are pending. Your data stays available offline on the web too.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_11": "Home screen widgets: Notes, Tasks and Calendar to see your latest notes, tasks to do and the next two weeks of plans; Quick actions and the round Note, Task and Event buttons to create a new item right away.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_12": "The app is also available in Italian: it follows your phone's language, or you can choose it in Settings > Language. Dates, pickers and system menus follow the app language.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_13": "Getting-started guide on first launch, always available from About Noteep. The About page is refreshed, with the main features, links to the source code and the developer, and the open-source licenses, fonts included.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_14": "Side menu with Calendar, Tasks, Notes and a dedicated Statistics section. In Settings, choose which section the app opens on, and pick theme and language with side-by-side buttons.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_15": "A more polished, consistent look: new icon and logo, a masonry notes grid with no gaps, a list preview while loading, smoother animations (turned off when the system reduces motion) and the same style for headers, settings and items across the app.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_16": "Accessibility: with TalkBack each note is read in full and quick actions are in the Actions menu; with very large system text nothing gets cut off. The first letter of titles and text is capitalized automatically.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_17": "Privacy policy in English and Italian, readable without an account and shown with the minimum age before signing up; it states that your content is stored on servers in the United States. In Settings you can permanently delete your account with all your data.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_18": "Backup restore and calendar import are safer: a selected file can no longer be used to reach other files on the device.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_19": "If startup fails, a message with a Retry button appears instead of a blank screen. After reinstalling, you stay signed in. Signing out stops that account's reminders and signing in schedules them again, even on a new device.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_20": "Importing a full backup now really removes the items that are not part of it. In ICS files, repeating events keep their end date and last occurrence, and times with a time zone stay correct.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_21": "Pinned notes and tasks always stay at the top; formatted notes show clean text, without asterisks or hash signs; tasks with a due time, for example imported from Google Tasks, keep their time.",
  "changelog_v2_0_0_bullet_22": "Notifications for tasks and events already on your account, restored from a backup or imported from a calendar file now arrive after signing in or restarting the app too, not just for the ones created or edited on the phone.",
